    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDomain",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDomain",
      "dcterms:title": "GDHCN Trust Domain",
      "dcterms:description": "A GDHCN Trust Domain. Its parts follow the definition in Section II of the GDHCN Administrative and Operational Framework, which says a Trust Domain consists of:\n\n- defined use cases and business processes related to the utilization of Verifiable Digital Health Certificates;\n- the open, interoperable technical specifications that identify or define the applicable Trusted Services and Verifiable Digital Health Certificates; and\n- a set of policy and regulatory standards describing expected behavior of GDHCN Participants.\n\nA Trust Domain also names its terms of use. This is the ValueSet of policies a participant may say it acts under, for example in the `termsOfUse` of a VHL Receiver's Verifiable Credential (see [TrustDomainPolicy](StructureDefinition-TrustDomainPolicy.html)).",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust/StructureDefinition/TrustDomain"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDomain.json"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "StructureDefinition-TrustDomainPolicy",
      "@type": "fhir:StructureDefinition",
      "dcterms:identifier": "StructureDefinition/TrustDomainPolicy",
      "dcterms:title": "GDHCN Trust Domain policy (VC termsOfUse entry)",
      "dcterms:description": "One entry of a W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model 2.0 `termsOfUse` (section 5.5) naming a policy of a GDHCN Trust Domain that the credential's issuer acts under. One example is a VHL Receiver's self-issued credential under the Verifiable Credential Option of IHE ITI VHL ITI-YY5.\n\nVC 2.0 requires each `termsOfUse` value to have a `type` and allows an `id`. The `type` is this logical model's canonical URL. The `id` is the policy: a code in a Trust Domain's terms-of-use ValueSet, written as `{CodeSystem canonical}#{code}`. A verifier finds the Trust Domain from the ValueSet that holds the policy.\n\n```json\n\"termsOfUse\": [{\n  \"type\": \"http://smart.who.int/trust/StructureDefinition/TrustDomainPolicy\",\n  \"id\": \"http://smart.who.int/ips-pilgrimage/CodeSystem/IPS.HAJJ.CONSENT#CONSENT-KSA\"\n}]\n```",
      "dcterms:type": "Structures: Logical Models",
      "schema:sameAs": {
        "@id": "http://smart.who.int/trust/StructureDefinition/TrustDomainPolicy"
      },
      "schema:contentUrl": {
        "@id": "../StructureDefinition-TrustDomainPolicy.json"
      }
    },
